<node id="1185510" title="Re^5: regex syntax and idomatic Perl" created="2017-03-22 19:33:06" updated="2017-03-22 19:33:06" _doctext_mode="lenient"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="1183826">cbeckley</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;p&gt;
For the record, I stared at that piece of code for an entire beer.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
So ... $_ in the for loop, and $y are references ...
&lt;br&gt; and you could have said
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;code&gt;
substr $x,5,3 =~ s/g/G/;
&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
Instead of
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;code&gt;
my $y = \substr $x,5,3;
$$y=~s/g/G/;&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
For the same result?
&lt;/p&gt;
</doctext>
